# Auto commit + push to main

After completing any meaningful code change in this repo:

1. Commit on `main` (do not create `cursor/` feature branches unless the user explicitly asks).
2. Use a concise commit message focused on why.
3. Immediately `git push origin main`.
4. Do not ask for confirmation for routine commits/pushes — the user requested this habit.
5. Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials). Never force-push.
6. Skip empty commits if there is nothing to stage.
